# MadGraph5 batch script: b b~ > h NP<=1
# in SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme (UFO v3.0.2), restricted by restrict_vg_cbH.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   O_bH gives an FFS vertex whose Lorentz structure is the bare `Identity(2,1)`
#   (SMEFTsim's FFS2) -- the one UFO operator no Standard-Model process reaches,
#   since the SM Yukawa vertex carries the same structure only through a coupling
#   the massless-lepton rows switch off.
#
#   2 -> 1 at fixed beams: the beams sit at MH/2, so the whole phase space is the
#   single point the amplitude table banks. MadEvent has no volume to integrate
#   and its `launch` stops after building the matrix element and libmodel.a,
#   which is everything the amplitude and diagram banks read.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/, which is where the
# vg_* restrict cards of validation/madgraph/cards/smeft/ are placed. Both
# generators therefore prune vertices from the same card.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# Orders are explicit because SMEFTsim gives NP hierarchy 99: MadGraph's default
# WEIGHTED bound would drop every diagram carrying a Wilson coefficient.
import model validation/ufo/SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme_UFO-vg_cbH
display interactions
generate b b~ > h NP<=1
output bbx_to_h_identity -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 62.545
set ebeam2 62.545
set use_syst False
done
